# .env.local
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values.
#
# No environment variables are required for the HRI engine itself.
# The app runs entirely through its internal /api/analyze route with
# no external backend — NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL and FASTAPI_URL previously
# documented here were never read anywhere in the code and have been
# removed.
#
# If/when a variable is actually wired up in code, document it here.

# Optional. Neon Postgres connection string for Observation Console
# logging (POST /api/log) AND the Notice system (Landing announcements,
# /admin/notices). When unset, /api/log runs as an honest no-op
# (persisted:false) and Notice reads/writes all fail soft (empty
# Landing notice list, "DATABASE_URL is not configured" in admin) — the
# HRI conversation is unaffected either way. Two separate tables, one
# connection string: see src/lib/observation/schema.sql and
# src/lib/notice/schema.sql for what each expects — run BOTH manually
# against Neon (the app never issues DDL itself).
# DATABASE_URL=

# Optional. Shared secret required to view /admin, /admin/observations,
# and /admin/notices (?key=<value>), and to bypass site closure below
# via /?key=<value>. When unset, all admin pages always return 404
# regardless of what key is supplied, and Notice admin writes always
# reject.
# ADMIN_ACCESS_KEY=

# Optional. Controls whether the public HRI site is reachable.
# "closed" shows a temporary-closure notice to everyone except an
# administrator with the correct ADMIN_ACCESS_KEY (via /?key=<value>).
# Any other value (or unset) behaves as "open".
# SITE_ACCESS_MODE=open
